{"type":"reasoning","id":"0c2827ad-68dd-4c58-9abd-b4bf17368888","text":"I'm running an adversarial check on partition boundaries with repeated call IDs—the loop breaks correctly at episode boundaries, but I'm noticing that when an assistant's tool_calls don't match the expected set, it gets silently dropped during pruning, including its partial tool results, which isn't an issue in pass-through mode but matters for the mandatory trailing logic.\n\nThere's also an edge case where a trailing assistant message with pending tool_calls and no results gets dropped entirely since it's not mandatory, which seems unusual but acceptable for interrupted sessions. On the token estimation side, the byte-based heuristic overestimates for English text (roughly 3 bytes/token vs real ~4 chars/token), meaning the 400k target is conservative but safe against the hard 460800 threshold, just wasting some context budget. I'm also noting that the sanitize-reflected logic could be quadratic on large prompts since it iterates over reflected parts times splitlines of a multi-megabyte prompt.\n\nOn redaction cost: each part gets passed through `_redact_secrets` with multiple regex passes across several variants, and since this only runs on the error path, the overall cost is bounded even for large prompts, though `_diagnostic_text` calling `_prompt_reflected_parts` four times with redaction applied twice per call could add noticeable latency on a 1.5MB prompt during failures. This is a scalability concern worth measuring quickly rather than something urgent.\n\n","timestamp":1791994950722,"session_id":"d310f7c6-395c-4c9d-b4f3-453a867f71bf"}
{"type":"tool_call","id":"toolu_01VdzYvHMNH6DJ7euEWt8mmv","messageId":"0c2827ad-68dd-4c58-9abd-b4bf17368888","toolId":"Execute","toolName":"Execute","parameters":{"summary":"Measure error-path sanitization cost on large prompt","command":"cd /Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport importlib.util, time\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"m\",\"bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\")\nm=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(m)\nmsgs=[]\nfor i in range(6000):\n    msgs.append({\"role\":\"user\" if i%2==0 else \"assistant\",\"content\":f\"line {i} \"+\"текст абв \"*30+\"\\nsecond line of message %d with data\"%i})\n_,_,p=m._assemble_prompt(msgs)\nprint(len(p))\nt=time.monotonic(); m._turn_diagnostics({\"terminal\":\"failed\",\"error\":{\"kind\":\"k\",\"message\":\"upstream failed\",\"quota\":{\"a\":1}},\"reason\":\"r\"},p); print(\"turn_diag\",round(time.monotonic()-t,2))\nt=time.monotonic(); m._sanitize_reflected(\"serve exited rc=1: boom\",[p],msgs); print(\"sanitize\",round(time.monotonic()-t,2))\nEOF","riskLevel":"low","timeout":180},"timestamp":1791994950722,"session_id":"d310f7c6-395c-4c9d-b4f3-453a867f71bf"}
